<title>USA: TABLE - Doncasters Plc Q2 sales, ADS rise.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Doncasters Plc Q2 sales, ADS rise.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>(U.K. GAAP)</p>
<p>					Second quarter	First half</p>
<p>					1997	1996     1997    1996</p>
<p>					(in thousands)    (in thousands)</p>
<p>Net sales (in pounds)     34,102	28,325   66,792   53,813</p>
<p>Costs and expenses:</p>
<p>Cost of sales		 26,829	22,735   52,849   42,834</p>
<p>Selling, general and</p>
<p> administration		2,383	 1,838    4,785    3,790</p>
<p>Depreciation		   1,037	 1,016    2,127    2,119</p>
<p>Total costs and expenses  30,249	25,589   59,761   48,743</p>
<p>Operating income	     3,853	 2,736    7,031    5,070</p>
<p>Net interest and other</p>
<p> income (expense)		186	    56	291	 98</p>
<p>Income before income taxes 4,039	 2,792    7,322    5,168</p>
<p>Income taxes		  (1,441)	 (784)  (2,619) (1,651)</p>
<p>Net income		     2,598	 2,008    4,703    3,517</p>
<p>Dividend			     0	     0     (600)	 0</p>
<p>Retained net income (pounds) 2,598     2,008    4,103    3,517</p>
<p>Net income per Ordinary</p>
<p> Share (pounds)		 0.15	  0.13     0.27     0.22</p>
<p>(Note 1)</p>
<p>Net income per ADS (pounds) 0.30	  0.26     0.54     0.44</p>
<p>(Note 1)</p>
<p>Net income per Ordinary Share</p>
<p> (Note 2)			$0.25	 $0.22    $0.45    $0.37</p>
<p>(Note 1)</p>
<p>Net income per ADS (Note 2)$0.50	 $0.44    $0.90    $0.74</p>
<p>(Note 1)</p>
<p>Ordinary Shares outstanding</p>
<p>  (in thousands)	    17,600	16,000   17,308   16,000</p>
<p>(Note 1)</p>
<p>ADS's outstanding (weighted</p>
<p> average, in thousands)    8,800	 8,000    8,654    8,000</p>
<p>(Note 1)</p>
<p>NOTES: (1) Historical share and income per share information for 1996 not considered meaningful due to reorganization in November and December 1996.</p>
<p>To provide a more meaningful comparison, Q2 and first half 1996 share and per share information is based on the number of Ordinary Shares in issue at Dec. 31, 1996. ADS and income per ADS information is calculated by adjusting the share data by the ratio of two Ordinary Shares per ADS.</p>
<p>As of June 30, 1997 there were 8.8 million ADS's issued representing 17.6 million Ordinary Shares.</p>
<p>(2) Dollar Net income per Ordinary Share and Dollar Net income per ADs calculated by translating pounds sterling into U.S. dollars at rate of 1.00 pound = $1.6650 (the noon buying rate on June 30, 1997).</p>
